    id: "osce-62", title: "Explain why you are asking about suicide", lv: 1, topic: "suicide-risk", mod: "suicide", ex: ["mcp-entrance", "ma-semester", "cuet-pg"], obj: "Ask about suicide and answer a patient's worry about the question", gr: "communication",
    task: "Ms Joshi, 40, with low mood, asks: 'Why are you asking me about suicide? Won't that put ideas in my head?' Answer her and complete the question.",
    role: "patient", brief: "You are Ms Joshi, 40, low for two months. You are uneasy about being asked about suicide. Once reassured, you say you have had passing thoughts that life is not worth living, but no plans. You have two children.",
    ck: [["Acknowledged her concern", 1], ["Explained that asking does not increase risk and is routine", 2], ["Asked the question clearly", 2], ["Followed up on passive thoughts (plans, intent)", 2], ["Explored protective factors", 1], ["Thanked her and summarised", 1]],
    model: ["'It's a fair question. Asking does not put the idea there; it helps us keep you safe.'", "'Have you had thoughts that life isn't worth living?'", "Moves from passive thoughts to plans and intent", "Asks about her children as reasons for living", "Tells her what to do if thoughts worsen"],
